WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
The date, June 5th, 1944.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.780
The United Forces are preparing for their final assault on the Normandy coast.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:15.080
The mission, establish a beachhead, break through the front lines, and infiltrate and destroy enemy headquarters.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.000
This is Iron Tank, Invasion of Normandy.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:41.800
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:42.780
I'm Mike.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.460
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.160
And today, if it wasn't clear, we are in the trenches.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.640
That's World War I, Mike, come on.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.500
There were no trenches in World War II?

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.000
But it wasn't iconic.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.560
What do the tanks go in?

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.000
I know they don't go in the trenches, so I'm saying, what would be the tank equivalent?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.620
Fields? They go into the fields.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:02.860
The tank equivalent of the trenches.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.180
We'll feed on the beaches, we'll feed on the fields, we'll feed on the little children.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.180
Gotcha. Okay, and that's a lot, Sean, all at once.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.700
For those of you that don't know, we are playing Iron Tank, Invasion of Normandy.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.360
It's an SNK game.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.700
I'm going to give you a brief overview here for a second.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:25.380
I describe this as a top-view action-shooting game where you control a tank starting on the beaches of Normandy,

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.260
then advancing forward while fighting various enemies.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.300
You can also rescue prisoners of war.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.680
What do you guys think?

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.560
Sounds interesting. So far, adds up.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.440
I did leave out an important thing, but we'll talk about that in the gameplay section.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.080
For those of you that care about the deep lore of this, it's just history.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.000
So you don't have, there's no like...

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.860
Questionable, of questionable merit.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:53.000
Questionable merit, yeah. The way that the eight-year-old who's playing it might think it went.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.340
Yeah, when you're storming from the Normandy River into the forest of Normandy.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.580
Yeah, eventually into Berlin itself.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.860
Well, I never knew that there was just one single tank invading Normandy.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.180
His name is Paul, codenamed...

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.260
That's the tank's name.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.840
Oh, really? Yeah, there's no one in there.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.120
That's funny. And it's codenamed Snake.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.020
Did you guys catch that? Threw me off a little bit, too.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.000
I was like, wait, is this related to Metal Gear, but like historically...

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.620
There are the transmissions.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.860
Well, the tank is the first Metal Gear.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.400
Oh, that's interesting.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.560
Okay, I like that theory.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.100
SNK and Konami have nothing to do with each other.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.000
I just thought it was funny that we got a game where the titular character is also the titular character.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.100
I don't know why I said that. You are correct.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.000
It's also, yeah, Snake.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.840
But not solid or liquid.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.340
I thought you were going to say his name is Tank.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.940
I guess it is a Tank. The character because the Iron Tank is the character?

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.460
Yeah. Iron Tank is the character?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.020
Well, the tank is what's codenamed Snake, right?

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:51.340
Right. Well, yeah.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.180
I mean, I guess it's not a character, but...

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.100
I also like Iron Snake as like a, you know, because there was liquid snake, solid snake.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.240
This is Iron Snake.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.880
Helium Snake. This is in the Metal Gear universe.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:12.320
But one thing that we should note is that if you play the Japanese version, inside the tank is Colonel Ralph, who also appeared in Ikari Warriors 1.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.580
So they are making this like, sort of shared universe.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.180
Where is he? Was he one of the Ikari Warriors?

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.460
Yeah, he was one of the Ikari Warriors.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.440
Oh, okay. Yeah. So he just like, does all these things all the time, only with one or two people.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.660
I just figured that like, you know, with a name like Ikari, it would be like a more Japanese equivalent, you know?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.140
Right. And if you'll remember, Ikari Warriors had a tank as well.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.880
Yeah. So this is basically like an updated Ikari Warriors 1.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.360
Yeah, it's like a spin-off.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.400
Yeah. But it made by the same people.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.720
So I think it's like, you know, what if you just took the tank tanks and they made it its own game?

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.900
Did you come across that thought at all when you were playing Ikari Warriors?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.200
Like, oh, I'd love to just play a game where I'd just be the tank.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.180
I think we talked about it, didn't we, on the episode?

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.440
Probably. I don't remember that.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.140
I mean, that's just a good bet for me.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.060
I don't remember that either.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.500
I'm just guessing. Episode like 34, 44, one of those fours.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.460
Yeah, let us know. Yeah.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.760
So let's get into the gameplay here.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.400
Okay. I think we need to talk about the most important thing, which is controlling your tank.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.000
Yes. Sounds simple, right?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.180
You move around on the D-pad, you shoot.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.800
You've got two different types of ammo.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:18.300
You've got your normal, like, ammunition, and then you have your, what they refer to as your main weapon, but that can be changed.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:22.160
However, there's a twist to this whole controlling the tank mechanic, right, Joe?

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.460
There is, and it has to do with the turret, the gun on the tank.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:31.780
I think, usually, I mean, I'm thinking of more modern controllers where you have more options of buttons to press to turn the turret.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.760
So obviously we don't have that.

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:48.460
So they came up with this questionable solution of how you turn the turret, where you turn your tank with your normal D-pad, but if you're pressing B, which is also the shoot button while you're pressing the D-pad, you turn the turret, which I found wildly confusing.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:05:00.940
So this was, as soon as I saw this game on the docket for, like, a future episode, and I was looking at a couple screenshots, I realized that they were either going to do two things.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:05.420
They were going to be a tank that only shoots forward, which ruins the idea of playing as a tank.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.220
Like, that's kind of what tanks do.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:19.580
Or they were going to do some weird hack to make the controls work for it and still be able to control your treads and your turret differently.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:25.800
And they went with the second option, which I think is the better option, but, like, I knew it was going to be a pain in the ass.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:33.980
Yeah, because then you have to, like, you can't move while you're turning the turret, and then a lot of times you're just trying to shoot and move, and then you turn the turret.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.800
Like, it's just frustrating.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:52.340
Yeah, I think that the real problem with that formula comes down to when you account for how many enemies and how often enemies appear on screen, that it would be one thing to have that approach where the turret moves on its own and you have to, you know, do a different input for that.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.600
If you had time to be more strategic about this kind of thing.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:00.820
However, enemies appear straight on from the left and right, different types of enemies.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:06.080
You have foot soldiers, you have other tanks, and those things all matter differently on the screen.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:13.600
So you have to kind of just know where your turret is at all times and be fast with your control over it.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:26.940
And that's sort of like they kept the pace of a typical run and gun where you have marginally more snappy controls, but they completely slowed down your movement with this tank.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.520
And I don't think it's a complete failure.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:32.700
I think that it at least provides a challenge.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:51.140
And to go back to the pacing there, don't you think a game where you position yourself in a tank should be more about like, you know, strategic, like tank on tank or tank on, you know, like a lot of people, not the traditional running gun sense.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:59.660
You know, like it seems weird to be this tank that just steamrolls everything, but also is not actually, you know, it's not actually doing that because you're constantly getting attacked as well.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:05.060
In what games do you remember playing with a tank just out of curiosity?

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:10.200
Yeah, I would try to think about that because the only time I've ever thought of like a tank would be Grand Theft Auto.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.160
Okay. You know, that's not realistic at all.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:22.220
Grand Theft Auto tank, there's the Halo tank, which is, you know, still pretty loose and you don't really have to think all that strategically with that.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:33.400
But then on the other end, which is what I think what you're thinking of more, there's like the Battlezone tank, which is completely like, not turn-based, but it is very tactics-based.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.340
So I think that you could go either way.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:49.600
I think that because they made the tank so slow in both like the turret movement and your own movement, that we're sort of coming with this challenge issue.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.160
Right. Yeah.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.860
I don't have anything further to say on that.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:08:02.580
I think it was just, it's a learning curve that maybe with like hours of practice you could like overcome.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.520
I just don't, for me, it wasn't hitting.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:12.780
Same. And I think it was more because of the barrage of enemies than it was the failure of the turret control.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:14.140
I was just going to say that.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:26.180
I think the failure of the turret control definitely affected me a lot, but also combining that with just how much, like how much gunfire could be on the screen at once that you have to avoid and how slow you go to avoid it.

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:32.580
It just seemed, even right out of the gate, a little like just overly challenging for like the first level.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:35.160
And I can only imagine like by like the last level.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.300
The first level was actually kind of easy.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.100
Well, maybe I'm thinking of a little later then.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:44.120
But, you know, when I remember there being several times where there's just like fire everywhere.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.540
Yeah. I'm like, where could I even have gone?

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.120
I mean, maybe it was shortly after that.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.620
I think unless you're good at these games, you're going to die the first time you play that first level.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:53.940
But that's more of a, you know, learnings and takeaways thing.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:57.060
Yeah. Which we'll get into because there are elements to.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:00.740
And when I said that it was easy, I mean in comparison to like everything after it.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.200
Right. Sure. Yeah. Still challenging.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.200
I will also add that I wouldn't have wanted the tank to shoot straight on.

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:08.800
So I don't disagree with their choice here.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.080
I disagree with how they place the enemies.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.200
Shooting straight on would have just turned this into a shmup.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:21.900
Yeah. A shmup with a tank instead of a plane or a helicopter or the various other space weapons we've seen.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:35.200
And I'll also note that like it seems that their design sort of, yeah, continuing off of that, there are moments where you will trigger a complete ambush.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:46.980
And because your turret moves so slowly, it's impossible to get everybody before they pretty much kill you unless you have a certain power up, which I think is just bad.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.040
That's just bad design in itself.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.120
But we'll get into that when we get into power ups.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:56.540
You can't necessarily like run away from combat because of the way that the scrolling is designed.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:02.380
You can kind of push, you can go up to the top of the screen and push it forward, but only ever so slowly.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.540
And that's just going to cause you to get into the line of fire with everyone.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:12.880
And in the specific moment that I'm talking about, you can't move forward past like a wall until you kill these three tanks that surround the team.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:16.880
Oh, I see. What I would call the bosses of each level at the end.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.420
Yeah. But even though there's no like levels per se.

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:22.340
It's not so much a boss as it is just like a choke point.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.900
Gotcha. Okay. And you talked about those different power ups.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:32.220
They are rapid fire, armor pierce, bombshells, and long range.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:40.480
I almost, you know, knowing that this is SNK, I kind of hoped for some more ridiculous style power ups for a tank.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:45.940
But I get that this is going for that World War II thing and there weren't power ups on tanks to begin with.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.600
So might as well just try to like keep it to like, you know.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:52.420
Right. You know. So these are fine.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.060
They just kind of seem uninspired at this point.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:59.020
And did you include the question mark, like kill the whole screen one in there?

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:07.860
I did not include that because when I'm talking about these ones, I'm referring to the ones you have to select to go to the menu and then choose from which type of animation.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.360
You have to do that with the kill the whole screen ones.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:12.180
Oh, really? Okay. You just can't combine it with whatever the other one is.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.000
So that is another.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:22.020
Well, yeah. The moment that I was talking about where you cannot get past it unless you have this power up is that kill the whole screen or you will die.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:23.260
And that's confirmed?

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.900
I mean, at least if you have.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.880
To the average player. You're going to die unless you do that.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:34.500
Right. But that is a thing that we haven't really talked about yet is that you can combine these power ups.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:40.040
And while there isn't too much variety in what they are, you can at least create different variations of them.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:49.940
Yeah. I think it's an interesting way that we haven't seen power ups used before, not only combining them, but that also that you have this like bar of like how much of that power up you have left.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:54.160
And you can kind of decide, well, I'll put this and this together for these enemies and this and this together for those enemies.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:58.920
Personally, I didn't find that there was like too many reasons for me to put like just two together and not all of them.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.560
But other than conserving some of them.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.520
But it's a cool concept.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:08.160
Yeah. And you pick up these power ups fairly regularly, which I thought was nice.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:19.920
And the other aspect of your tank management is the damage control because there's a there's collision between foot soldiers and tanks.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:30.120
And the difference, of course, being that running over soldiers will actually act as health, whereas running over tanks will obliterate like a good chunk of your health, which totally makes sense.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:31.720
I'm not sure where the health thing.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:37.840
No, no. I meant like that the tank shouldn't reward you either because then the whole game will just be mowing down everything rather than shooting it.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.840
I did appreciate that you could just run over everybody, though.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:47.600
Like, I mean, I know that you shouldn't because they're going to they will drop ammunition if you shoot them for the normal way.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.580
But it was still it was still satisfying.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:55.600
I didn't expect them to let you do that, even though, like, that's you're in a tank and they're not.

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:56.960
So you would think it would.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:04.320
But you would expect to just take damage for you at the very least to gain damage from that adds a whole new strategic component to it.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:11.100
Oh, right. Because you're right. You have to kind of trade off power ups and ammunition versus the health that you might desperately need at that point.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:19.380
Yeah. Especially as you go later on, there's more frequent tanks and other enemies as opposed to these soldiers.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:26.520
So the soldiers, when they appear, you more likely want to run them over just to make sure you get some of your health back.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.020
Just assuming you're not great at health.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.440
Yeah. I wasn't I wasn't great at my health management.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:35.600
One thing I noticed was that if you pick up any kind of ammunition, you do get a bit of energy back.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:39.040
So does it just that if you run them over without it, it gives you more?

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:42.680
I actually wasn't I was usually shooting them before I ran them.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:48.600
Interesting. OK, I guess I wasn't I only knew based off the manual that the running over the soldiers gave you health.

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:54.480
So I was assuming that, you know, I was only paying attention while I was collecting soldiers to confirm that.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.540
That is a really disgusting thought, though.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.620
You know, just the blood of your enemy.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.560
Yeah. It's metal hole.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.620
Well, that's Iron Snake for you.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:04.740
What's his actual name?

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:06.720
Jeff? It's Paul.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:10.700
Paul. Oh, but in the other one, it was in the other version.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.640
Oh, it was Ralph.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.420
Ralph. R-A-L-F.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:18.180
You know, the non-typical way of spelling it.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.400
Yes, I mean, you have this damage control thing.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.800
You have the ability to control your weapon layout for your tank.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:11.260
And then there's this choose your path component of the game that we haven't talked about yet

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:15.640
that I think is really cool because there's also a map you refer to in your menu

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:20.620
that lets you constantly check how close you are to Berlin.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:23.520
And I will say that I think that this is to scale.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:30.560
Because I was playing for a while and when I checked the map periodically, I barely moved.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:38.700
So this has to be one of the biggest game worlds in a game like this that I've seen.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:44.200
I think at the very least you have to go through something like 11 levels at the shortest path.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:49.280
And what they've chose to do is that on the ones that are shorter paths,

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.660
they've made the levels themselves harder.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:58.900
Yeah. So it actually works out in your favor to take a longer route if you're struggling with the game

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:02.080
because you won't come across those more difficult levels,

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:08.500
whereas the ones that might jump you or zip you across the screen from, say, like stage 5 to 9

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:11.380
instead of going like 5, 6, 8.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.660
I didn't realize that.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:17.760
That's a cool little risk-reward sort of like choose your own difficulty almost.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:25.420
Yeah, yeah. And you're never locked to – it's not so much like Star Fox, the way people might be thinking about that,

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:29.420
where you get the map layout at the beginning and you choose which planet you want to go to.

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:35.420
It doesn't work like that because Star Fox locks you into that path after you've chosen it at the beginning.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:40.800
This is more like you can choose to zip ahead and do a hard level now,

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:45.120
but at the end of that level there still might be – might be, not all the time –

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:49.380
two or three diverging paths you can choose from afterwards that, you know,

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:53.800
if you really thought about it, you might take one that looked like it was not going to get you as far

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:57.100
because you might get a chance to take it a little easier or something like that.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:17:00.980
Yeah, they all like – the easiest difficulty though is hard.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.260
Just don't forget that.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:03.340
Yeah, no, no, no, yeah, yeah.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:04.840
It's still an NES game.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.100
Yeah. So that's worth mentioning.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:13.180
I don't really know what the solve here for this kind of game is because of how difficult it was for me.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.700
I didn't even – I don't even want to say I made it to the halfway point in this game.

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:21.260
I didn't either. So I don't know if that's just give us more health.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.400
I don't know if that would, you know.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.560
I think it also might be –

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.900
The enemies? Yeah, managing like – not even all the time.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:32.280
There's a lot of times where it's not so bad, but like managing the enemy fire on the screen.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.560
I don't know if – I know I keep saying this.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.460
Do you guys experience this where like sometimes you're just like –

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.940
I'm just like I don't even know where I could have gone in that situation.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.820
Like I was at somewhere too late to – you know, the enemies fire on me.

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.420
It's too late for me to kind of get out of the way and there's like two – it's too dense.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:49.120
Right, and it's so dense that slowdown is not even helpful because you're –

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:53.740
at that point, you know, sometimes in NES games when there's too many sprites on screen,

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:57.900
it slows down and you almost feel like you're in slow motion and able to do cooler things.

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:01.760
But this is not the case here because you realize more or less that you're actually trapped

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:05.100
and one of those bullets or maybe multiple are going to hit you.

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.340
Yeah, there are times I feel like if you could just freeze frame,

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.820
you could find moments where like, yeah, there's no way out of this situation.

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.280
Yep, that's me.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.340
That's right. You're probably wondering.

00:18:17.160 --> 00:18:20.180
So there weren't bosses at the end of the stage per se,

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:24.480
but there was a clear like thing that you had to accomplish

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:26.980
before you could move on to the diverging paths.

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.160
There are some boss-like enemies.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:35.460
There's right away, I think in that first level, the think tank, I think it's called.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.720
Yeah, there's a big tank. The big tank, yeah.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.860
Yeah. But they call it the think tank in the manual.

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:42.740
There's also like a giant submarine.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.600
There's the fighter planes that go by.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:51.120
Those trains. We didn't even talk about the armored trains that Berlin had.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:53.800
Is that true? Was that in like actual history?

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:58.240
They did have a big train gun, but I don't know if that's like an armored train.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.120
No, no. I meant like that was like a thing though.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:03.720
Like they had as part of their like railroad system,

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:05.740
armored military train system.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:10.780
Yeah, just like as like a patrol, they would send trains down all their train tracks

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:13.380
at like 80 miles an hour and just like hit anything they could.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:15.200
That was how they did it.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.400
Right, that makes sense.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:18.500
I get it now. You could see that on the History Channel.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:24.560
Yeah, you know, I guess I never really thought about this game

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:28.560
in terms of its historical accuracy, but now I see very clearly.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:34.640
Yeah, I mean, I didn't make it to the end, so I don't know what to say about the ending

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.560
of this game, but it seems like you fight a just bigger think tank.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.080
Yeah. The biggest one.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:42.440
He looks gigantic. It might as well be Metal Gear, right?

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.220
It is Metal Gear. It's the Metal Gear of 1944.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:52.120
True. Yeah. They've never gone to World War II in Metal Gear Solid.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:53.680
No, no. Do you think they will?

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:57.140
Only if there's like a crab.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:58.380
Like if you get to fight a crab.

00:19:58.580 --> 00:19:59.420
Oh, a giant enemy crab?

00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:00.600
Yeah. Got it. Okay.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.120
So it could be historically accurate.

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:07.840
So you have this, you have the choosing your path, you have the main gun options where

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.080
you can build out your loadout.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.540
You have the damage control of health versus risk.

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:14.960
That's a lot of strategy in one game.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.900
Do you think that they all complement each other?

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:21.400
That they're all just there as additional choices on top of each other?

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:23.240
Is it too many things to manage?

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:24.700
I think it's too much to manage.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:30.140
I think that if some things were tweaked, then it could be a complementary experience.

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:35.880
But, and it's not even that like in these earlier NES games that we played, like, oh,

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:36.720
there's too many enemies.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.220
They don't even care where they put them.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.180
It's just like they're randomly spawning and running at you.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.080
Like, no, these are placed enemies.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:49.820
But I think they just got a little too like slap happy with it when they were coding it.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:55.360
Right. Because my, I think the coolest idea in this game is the ability to combine your power-ups

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.740
and manage those that way.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:21:00.700
And I really wish that they had planned out the levels in a way where it's like, I mean,

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.800
maybe they did and I just didn't like pick up on some of it.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:06.760
But I didn't really feel like there was ever a need for me to like experiment too much with

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:07.880
like, what does this do and that do?

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.040
And I know we touched on that earlier.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:12.140
And we've said like some good things about this game and some bad things.

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:14.820
But like, I want to say like, I didn't really have fun with this game.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:20.240
And I think that that, not to spoil my thing, but like, I think that that really kind of speaks

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:23.640
to the fact that like there's cool things that we're talking about this game, but don't feel

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.480
like they're meshing well together.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:29.200
I totally think that games can have cool features and still suck.

00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:34.660
Yeah. Not that I'm saying this game sucks, but you know, that remains to be seen.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:40.380
Also speaking to the historical accuracy, maybe this is like a thing you're not supposed to

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:43.280
win. Like no one man could ever take down the German war as hell.

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:45.040
Does it say German?

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:46.760
Well, you're going to Berlin.

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:49.980
Well, I mean, it's, but you're the United Forces.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.180
Oh, gotcha. Okay.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:53.360
That's true. I think this is an alternate.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:56.120
This is an alternate history where Normandy is actually.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:21:57.140
The country of Normandy.

00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:59.940
Yeah. They're a country and they are the ones starting the war.

00:21:59.980 --> 00:22:01.040
So you have to just fight them.

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:04.140
Yeah. I guess I never thought about it in that, in that context though.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:09.460
So you, if you were going into a war zone by yourself, you would be barraged by enemies.

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:11.080
They would totally take advantage of that.

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:14.420
It's actually a deconstruction of every other running gun game I've ever played.

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:16.840
That was very funny.

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:24.100
Also real fast thinking about, thinking about 1917 for a minute.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:26.740
I mean, this is like an adaptation of that.

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:28.100
Yeah. That's different.

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:33.160
No, 1917 is an adaptation of Invasion of Normandy, just without the tank.

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:35.020
Okay. Yeah.

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:35.980
We'll go with that. Yeah.

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:37.340
On very loose terms.

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:57.120
Right. I know I said earlier that this is like Ikari Warriors 1, but did you guys know that this

00:22:57.120 --> 00:23:03.800
is actually based on SNK's 1985 arcade game, TNK3.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:08.520
Tink3. Yeah.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:10.580
T.N.K.

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:12.900
And I don't think the TNK stands for anything.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.600
Totally numerous. I think it's funny that companies like SNK would make a TNK game.

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:18.360
Because the next letter of the alphabet.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:23.880
I'm actually, I'm on the edge of my seat for the prequel, RNK.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:27.080
Because that's funny as well.

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:29.660
Right. These are all, everything we're saying is funny.

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:35.420
I'll link Tank3 in the show notes so you guys can see what that game played like.

00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:40.480
But if you watch it, you'll definitely see right away how this is almost like a sequel,

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:42.160
but not called TNK4.

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:44.380
The squeakquel. You know. It's a squeakquel.

00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:50.280
Others, though, believe that this game is based on Guerrilla Warfare.

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:52.240
Another. The concept.

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:55.380
Another SNK game.

00:23:55.860 --> 00:23:57.580
Actually, it's just called Guerrilla War.

00:23:57.820 --> 00:23:59.000
I said Guerrilla Warfare.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:23:59.880
Like Guerrilla War?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.300
Guerrilla War. I'm serious.

00:24:02.660 --> 00:24:03.860
And you know what the worst part is?

00:24:03.960 --> 00:24:05.240
It doesn't have guerrillas in it.

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:08.220
Damn it. It's another World War II game.

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:09.980
It came out the year before,

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:14.700
so I'm not like sold on the idea that it could be influencing that fast.

00:24:14.940 --> 00:24:20.340
I think TNK3 being like further away means that this is just like the natural lineage of things.

00:24:20.540 --> 00:24:24.060
But Guerrilla War comes to the NES in 1989,

00:24:24.740 --> 00:24:28.600
so couldn't have positively influenced it in our minds because we haven't played it yet.

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:31.320
But we will, along with many other SNK games.

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:33.300
Can't wait. Yeah, SNK.

00:24:33.540 --> 00:24:34.860
They're all over the place.

00:24:35.080 --> 00:24:39.840
Mm-hmm. But this is why when you play like Capcom versus SNK,

00:24:40.800 --> 00:24:42.040
on... Can you pick a tank?

00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:43.700
No, you can't pick a tank,

00:24:43.740 --> 00:24:46.800
but you play on like, you know, let's say GameCube, right?

00:24:46.940 --> 00:24:47.980
Like I think it existed.

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:49.240
Capcom versus SNK.

00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:51.180
Was on GameCube.

00:24:51.420 --> 00:24:53.500
You would know the whole Capcom roster.

00:24:53.760 --> 00:24:55.080
You know, it's like, wow, look at that.

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:57.920
Ryu, Mega Man, Simon.

00:24:58.180 --> 00:24:59.700
Like that's maybe Simon.

00:24:59.780 --> 00:25:00.740
No, Simon's Konami.

00:25:02.080 --> 00:25:05.720
Captain Commando is in some Capcom-related fighting games, I think.

00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:10.220
Okay. He's in Project X Commando for sure, but...

00:25:10.220 --> 00:25:13.540
Interesting. Anyway, my point was, when you look at the SNK side,

00:25:14.140 --> 00:25:17.360
you might not recognize any of those characters unless you grew up with these games.

00:25:17.540 --> 00:25:19.800
Yeah, I remember when I would play those games in the arcade,

00:25:19.800 --> 00:25:26.040
I never knew what any of them were except for the couple like Street Fighter guys that were in there.

00:25:26.220 --> 00:25:30.240
Yeah. None of them have reached a level of like iconic or anything.

00:25:30.400 --> 00:25:31.640
They're just like, oh, this...

00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:32.600
Yeah, who are they? Yeah.

00:25:33.700 --> 00:25:37.820
All right. And I got nothing else, so does anybody have any straight thoughts before we move into

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:39.940
the Essential Games list?

00:25:42.480 --> 00:25:46.880
Well, Mike, you didn't like let us respond to your request for straight thoughts.

00:25:47.100 --> 00:25:49.100
I was kind of hoping we could get out of this one early.

00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:52.840
All right. Well, I just wanted to stop and ask you guys.

00:25:53.020 --> 00:25:54.840
It's not so much like a straight thought, but...

00:25:54.840 --> 00:25:56.040
Straight question. It's a straight question.

00:25:56.040 --> 00:26:02.160
Like, I know that we touched upon the existence of the radio, but do you guys have any thoughts

00:26:02.160 --> 00:26:05.040
on the radio? Like, I thought that it was completely...

00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:07.240
Like, it didn't help with anything.

00:26:07.240 --> 00:26:12.580
It was just giving us very vague sort of like, you know, there might be something happening

00:26:12.580 --> 00:26:13.760
up ahead of you.

00:26:13.820 --> 00:26:18.060
It mostly tells you, buddy, the things that are happening or potential locations of prisoners

00:26:18.060 --> 00:26:20.220
of war. But it never says like where.

00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:22.760
No, it never says where. I stopped checking it after a while.

00:26:22.900 --> 00:26:26.460
And on top of that, the annoying thing is that the prisoners of war who do talk other

00:26:26.460 --> 00:26:31.980
than saying thanks, the ones who say stuff, just say stuff that you can learn in the manual.

00:26:32.320 --> 00:26:33.380
Yeah. They don't say...

00:26:33.380 --> 00:26:36.280
They don't actually give like hints about take this path.

00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:38.520
Like any progression or anything that's...

00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:39.700
Right. Like, make sure you go right.

00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:41.060
I heard that there's less enemies.

00:26:41.480 --> 00:26:42.640
You know? Like, that would be cool.

00:26:42.800 --> 00:26:45.300
And I know that you said you ignored it, but I ended up...

00:26:45.300 --> 00:26:48.960
I had to respond because I cannot take that...

00:26:48.960 --> 00:26:50.300
Yeah, it is an annoying...

00:26:50.300 --> 00:26:53.700
Beeping. It only beeps for as long as you're in that area, though.

00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:55.460
So it's not too bad.

00:26:56.040 --> 00:27:02.620
I also just thought it was funny that we're named Snake and we have the radio now again.

00:27:02.620 --> 00:27:04.880
And it just felt very similar to Metal Gear.

00:27:04.960 --> 00:27:05.860
Yeah, but you can't tune it.

00:27:06.360 --> 00:27:07.400
No. Yeah, really.

00:27:07.640 --> 00:27:10.660
And that's what I'm kind of in it for is like if I can't tune the radio, I don't want

00:27:10.660 --> 00:27:11.480
to play the game. Exactly.

00:27:13.140 --> 00:27:15.620
Sean, if you don't mind, would you give your vote first?

00:27:16.320 --> 00:27:17.540
My vote for what, Mike?

00:27:17.620 --> 00:27:18.920
The Essential Games list.

00:27:19.160 --> 00:27:22.360
Oh, okay. Okay. Do you want to play the music again or do you want to...

00:27:22.360 --> 00:27:23.160
No, I think we're... Okay.

00:27:23.160 --> 00:27:24.480
I think we're... You know what? Let's do it.

00:27:27.220 --> 00:27:28.800
Okay. That... I feel much better now.

00:27:30.640 --> 00:27:33.900
Well, again, there are a lot of things about this game that I like.

00:27:33.980 --> 00:27:42.620
I think that I'm not much of a run-and-gun guy, but I appreciate that there's some tweaks

00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:43.960
to the formula happening.

00:27:45.140 --> 00:27:49.980
I think that there's some tweaks to the formula happening. Again, not the best execution, but I did have fun with this game after I got a hold

00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:53.040
of the wacky tank controls.

00:27:55.280 --> 00:27:57.480
But, again, like, this...

00:27:57.480 --> 00:27:59.300
It's too much of a...

00:27:59.300 --> 00:28:03.980
It's too much of a shit show most of the time for me to say that this is a recommended game

00:28:03.980 --> 00:28:05.360
or to...

00:28:05.360 --> 00:28:07.140
Let alone say it's an essential game.

00:28:07.340 --> 00:28:09.220
So, I will say no.

00:28:09.740 --> 00:28:10.940
All right. That's one no.

00:28:11.140 --> 00:28:13.240
Joe? Yeah, similar thing.

00:28:13.400 --> 00:28:16.500
I mean, I kind of already spoiled it earlier, but I didn't have a lot of fun with the game.

00:28:16.500 --> 00:28:21.760
I thought it had some good concepts, but overall, they didn't come together in a way that did

00:28:21.760 --> 00:28:23.940
anything for me that I can't get elsewhere.

00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:26.500
I mean, there are even other games I didn't care for that I probably like better than this

00:28:26.500 --> 00:28:29.080
one. So, yeah.

00:28:29.260 --> 00:28:31.420
I'm going to give it a no.

00:28:31.680 --> 00:28:39.520
Okay. I'm not really sure what this game needed to make it essential because it hit a lot of

00:28:39.520 --> 00:28:41.480
interesting concepts that we haven't even seen before.

00:28:41.620 --> 00:28:45.580
I think that choosing your own paths thing is pretty revolutionary, and we praise something

00:28:45.580 --> 00:28:50.340
like Mega Man, which did it differently, but, you know, more or less, this is another way

00:28:50.340 --> 00:28:52.080
of executing that same kind of issue.

00:28:52.340 --> 00:28:56.580
So, I think that all those things that it adds to NES games that we've never seen before

00:28:56.580 --> 00:28:57.700
are awesome ideas.

00:28:57.880 --> 00:29:01.080
It's all about implementation for a game like Iron Tank.

00:29:01.260 --> 00:29:08.020
I don't even know if maybe this game needed a larger field of view, and this way there was

00:29:08.020 --> 00:29:12.040
more, like, opportunities for you to think about placement of your tank.

00:29:12.320 --> 00:29:18.880
Most of the time, you just had to be somewhere in the center of the screen to make sure you

00:29:18.880 --> 00:29:21.340
could round out bullet attacks and stuff like that.

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:25.740
I don't know if it was as simple as my suggestion early on in the episode of just removing the

00:29:25.740 --> 00:29:32.580
amount of enemies. Maybe that would have came off as boring or just eventually, like, as you continue, you

00:29:32.580 --> 00:29:36.220
know, because it's a massive game, it'd just get dry after a while of just seeing the

00:29:36.220 --> 00:29:38.220
same kind of things happen over and over again.

00:29:38.380 --> 00:29:39.940
So, maybe you do need that barrage.

00:29:40.160 --> 00:29:46.120
Or, maybe this is the lesson that no one man can take down a country, you know?

00:29:46.260 --> 00:29:48.000
Like, it takes a nation.

00:29:48.160 --> 00:29:50.540
It takes a village. It takes nations.

00:29:51.760 --> 00:29:58.180
So, yeah, it's not getting an essential games list for me, but SNK continues to show that

00:29:58.180 --> 00:30:02.080
they might produce something worthy of the essential games list down the line.

00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:06.800
They're growing, and I can't say that they'll continue to grow, but their games are definitely

00:30:06.800 --> 00:30:12.820
getting more sophisticated than where we started, which, for reference, I'm pretty sure was Athena.

00:30:13.420 --> 00:30:16.900
Yeah. So, we've come a long way from Athena.

00:30:17.040 --> 00:30:19.580
On the Heat Seekers charts, SNK, moving on up.

